        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market / liquidity",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The Virtuals ecosystem hit $3M monthly volume across 18K+ agents, but fragmented payment standards mean liquidity is siloed per rail; a dominant standard not emerging quickly keeps cross-agent settlement thin and volatile.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Governance / standards capture",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "ERC-7715, ERC-8004, and ERC-8183 are competing in parallel with no clear Ethereum-community consensus process, creating risk that whichever standard a major integrator (Etherscan, MetaMask) adopts by default becomes de facto law.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Operational / insider risk",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The Leviathan prediction market incident showed that agents marketed as autonomous can be operator-directed in ways that are invisible to counterparties, making insider trading structurally undetectable without onchain audit trails.",
          "source": ""
        }
